## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates hands-on understanding of tenant isolation within a shared infrastructure model and the ability to translate policy risks into pragmatic, automated security controls.

## Key Concepts
- S3 Block Public Access at bucket and account levels to prevent unintended public exposure
- Tenant-scoped IAM roles with `sts:AssumeRole` and attribute-based conditions for least-privilege access
- Per-tenant KMS Customer Master Keys with automated rotation for robust key management
- CloudTrail data events for S3 object-level audit logging and forensic analysis
- EventBridge-driven containment workflows for automated access revocation upon anomaly detection

